<article class="env-proposition" id="A3F6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/A3F6">Proposition <span data-tag="A3F6">8.1.5.12</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be presentable $\infty $-category, $\kappa $ a regular cardinal, $\overline{S}$ a weakly saturated class of morphisms in $\calC $. Let $S \subseteq \overline{S}$ be the subset consisting of those morphisms $f: X \rightarrow Y$ in $\overline{S}$ such that $X$ and $Y$ are $\kappa $-compact. Assume that: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(i)$"><p>
The regular cardinal $\kappa $ is uncountable, and $\calC $ is $\kappa $-accessible. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(ii)$"><p>
The set $S$ generates $\overline{S}$ as a weakly saturated class of morphisms. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
  <p> Then, for every morphism $f: X \rightarrow Y$ belonging to $\overline{S}$, there exists an transfinite sequence of objects $\{  Y_{\gamma } \} _{\gamma < \beta }$ of $\calC _{X/}$ with the following properties: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
For every ordinal $\gamma < \beta $, the natural map $\colim _{\gamma ' < \gamma } Z_{\gamma '} \rightarrow Z_{\gamma }$ is the pushout of a morphism in $S$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
The colimit $\colim _{\gamma < \beta } Z_{\gamma }$ is isomorphic to $Y$ (as objects of $\calC _{X/}$). 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Remark <a href="/tag/D48A" data-tag="D48A">8.1.2.8</a> implies the existence of a transfinite sequence of objects 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  Y_0 \rightarrow Y_1 \rightarrow \ldots  \]
</div>
    <p>
       in $\calC _{X/}$ indexed by a set of ordinals $A = \{  \alpha | \alpha < \lambda \} $, satisfying condition $(1)$, such that $Y$ is a <em>retract</em> of $\colim _{\alpha < \lambda } Y_{\alpha }$ in $\calC _{X/}$. We may view the sequence $\{  Y_{\alpha } \} _{ \alpha \in A}$ as an $S$-tree in $\calC $, having root $X$. According to Lemma <a href="/tag/A646" data-tag="A646">8.1.5.7</a>, we can choose a new $S$-tree $\{  Y'_{\alpha } \} _{ \alpha \in A'}$ which is $\kappa $-good, where $Y'_{A'} \simeq Y_ A$, so that $Y$ is a retract of $Y'_{A'}$. Choose an idempotent map $T_{A'}: Y'_{A'} \rightarrow Y'_{A'}$ in $\calC _{X/}$, whose image is isomorphic to $Y$. 
    <p>
      We now define a transfinite sequence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  B(0) \subseteq B(1) \subseteq B(2) \subseteq \ldots ,  \]
</div>
    <p>
       indexed by ordinals $\gamma < \beta $, and a compatible system of idempotent maps $T_{B(\gamma )}: Y'_{B_\gamma } \rightarrow Y'_{B_{\gamma }}.$ Fix an ordinal $\gamma $, and suppose that $B(\gamma ')$ and $T_{B(\gamma ')}$ have been defined for $\gamma ' < \gamma $. Let $B'(\gamma ) = \bigcup _{ \gamma ' < \gamma } B(\gamma ')$, and let $T_{B'(\gamma )}$ be the result of amalgamating the maps $\{  T_{B(\gamma ')} \} _{\gamma ' < \gamma }$. If $B'(\gamma ) = A'$, we set $\beta = \gamma $ and conclude the construction; otherwise, choose a minimal element $a \in A' - B'(\gamma )$. Applying Lemma <a href="/tag/191E" data-tag="191E">8.1.5.9</a>, we deduce the existence of a downward closed subset $C(\gamma ) \subseteq A'$, and a compatible collection of idempotent maps 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  T_{C(\gamma )} : Y'_{C(\gamma )} \rightarrow Y'_{C(\gamma )}  \]
</div>
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  T_{C(\gamma ) \cap B'(\gamma )}: Y'_{C(\gamma ) \cap B'(\gamma )} \rightarrow Y'_{C(\gamma ) \cap B'(\gamma )}. \]
</div>
    <p>
       We then define $B(\gamma ) = B'(\gamma ) \cup C(\gamma )$, and $T_{B(\gamma )}$ to be the result of amalgamating $T_{B'(\gamma )}$ and $T_{C(\gamma )}$. 
    <p>
      We observe that, for every ordinal $\gamma $, there is a $\kappa $-good $S$-tree $\{  Y''_{\alpha } \} _{ \alpha \in B(\gamma ) - B'(\gamma )}$ with root $Y'_{B(\gamma )}$, such that $Y''_{B(\gamma )-B'(\gamma )} \simeq Y'_{B(\gamma )}$ (Remark <a href="/tag/6346" data-tag="6346">8.1.5.5</a>). Combining Lemma <a href="/tag/C071" data-tag="C071">8.1.5.11</a> with the observation that $B(\gamma )-B'(\gamma )$ is $\kappa $-small, we deduce that the map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  Y'_{B'(\gamma )} \rightarrow Y'_{B(\gamma )} \]
</div>
    <p>
       is the pushout of a morphism in $S$. 
    <p>
      For each ordinal $\gamma < \beta $, let $Z_{\gamma }$ denote the image of the idempotent map $T_{B(\gamma )}$. Then $\colim _{\gamma < \beta } Z_{\gamma } \simeq Y$, so that $(2)$ is satisfied. Condition $(1)$ follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/646A" data-tag="646A">8.1.5.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>